# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the RetroPlug native host + test binaries.
#
# Keep this list MINIMAL and documented — each entry must name a known-benign
# race with a reason. Anything not listed here is treated as a real bug.
#
# Referenced via TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=... by tools/run-sanitizer.sh +
# tools/run-sanitizers.sh. Entries are added below as the actual TSan output requires them.

# Triple-buffer seqlock (MemorySnapshotTriple / FrameBufferTriple). The reader
# memcpy's a slot that the writer may be concurrently overwriting; the reader
# then re-reads the seqlock counter and DISCARDS the copy on mismatch (the
# stress tests assert zero torn reads). This is the standard seqlock pattern —
# UB on paper, benign in practice — so the non-atomic slot read is expected.
# Any real race elsewhere still surfaces; these only cover the readInto memcpy.
race:MemorySnapshotTriple::readInto
race:FrameBufferTriple::readInto

# efsw (vendored, deps/efsw) internal teardown race: FileWatcherInotify's destructor
# reads a status flag that its own watcher thread writes in handleAction as the thread
# winds down, without full synchronization. BOTH racing frames are efsw-internal — our
# NativeFileWatcher (which joins the thread via the efsw destructor, correctly ordered
# after our own members) is not in either access. Upstream code we don't own; benign on
# teardown. Scoped to the two named efsw functions so real races elsewhere still surface.
race:efsw::FileWatcherInotify::~FileWatcherInotify
race:efsw::FileWatcherInotify::handleAction
